<h1>Steg-Tool: Suggested Improvements and Implementation Plan</h1>
<p><strong>Generated:</strong> 2026-07-29</p>

<div class="section">
<h2>Program highlights (what this program does)</h2>
<ul>
<li>Steg-Tool is a Tkinter GUI for hiding and extracting payloads in images using AES-256-GCM and scrypt KDF.</li>
<li>Embedding uses LSB matching with a scatter permutation and a wire format labeled <code>&lt;|STEGv4|&gt;</code>.</li>
<li>Main components: GUI (Tkinter/TkinterDnD), image handling (Pillow), stego logic (numpy), crypto (pycryptodome scrypt & AES-GCM).</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>High-level change summary (prioritized)</h2>
<ol>
<li>Fix drag-and-drop path parsing to be cross-platform and robust.</li>
<li>Make DPI-awareness handling safer (avoid referencing undefined variables).</li>
<li>Use context managers for <code>Image.open</code> across the codebase to avoid leaked file handles.</li>
<li>Add structured logging and narrow broad <code>except</code> handlers (log tracebacks, keep friendly UI messages).</li>
<li>Make scrypt KDF parameters configurable via environment variables (and optionally UI).</li>
<li>Refactor core cryptographic & stego functionality into <code>steg_core.py</code> for testability and separation of concerns.</li>
<li>Add a minimal CLI for headless hide/extract flows.</li>
<li>Add unit tests (pytest) for core functionality using small images and reduced scrypt costs in CI/tests.</li>
<li>Add <code>requirements.txt</code> (or <code>pyproject.toml</code>) and CI workflow for tests.</li>
<li>UX improvements: warn about weak passwords, show confirmations, and maintain non-blocking UI flows.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>Branch & commit plan</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Branch name:</strong> <code>feat/refactor-hardening-stegtool</code></li>
<li><strong>Suggested commits:</strong>
<ul>
<li>feat(core): extract Stego/KDF/AESGCM/pack/unpack to <code>steg_core.py</code></li>
<li>fix(gui): robust drag &amp; drop path parsing and safer DPI handling</li>
<li>fix(io): use context managers for <code>Image.open</code>; add logging</li>
<li>feat(config): make scrypt params configurable via env vars</li>
<li>feat(cli & tests): add CLI entrypoint and unit tests</li>
<li>chore: add <code>requirements.txt</code> and CI workflow</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>PR title suggestion:</strong> Refactor core logic, harden file handling &amp; DnD, add logging, KDF config, CLI &amp; tests</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>Concrete file changes</h2>
<p>Below are the files to create/modify and the rationale.</p>

<h3>Create: <code>steg_core.py</code></h3>
<p>Move core logic (KDF, AESGCM, packing, LSB helper, Stego class) into a testable module. Keep public API compatible with existing calls from the GUI so integration is minimal.</p>

<pre><code># steg_core.py  (skeleton)
"""
Core steganography primitives for Steg-Tool
"""

from Crypto.Cipher import AES
from Crypto.Protocol.KDF import scrypt as _scrypt
import os, struct
import numpy as np

DELIM = b'<|STEGv4|>'
PLAIN_HDR = b'\xCE\xFB\x04\x01'
SALT_BITS = 256

class KDF:
    SALT_LEN = 32
    _N = int(os.getenv('STEG_SCRYPT_N', 2**17))
    _r = int(os.getenv('STEG_SCRYPT_r', 8))
    _p = int(os.getenv('STEG_SCRYPT_p', 1))

    @classmethod
    def derive(cls, pw: str, salt: bytes):
        km = _scrypt(pw.encode(), salt, key_len=64, N=cls._N, r=cls._r, p=cls._p)
        return km[:32], int.from_bytes(km[32:40], 'big')

# ... AESGCM, pack_text, pack_file, unpack, _lsb_match, Stego class ...
</code></pre>

<h3>Modify: <code>stegtool.py</code> (GUI)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Import from <code>steg_core</code> instead of having the Stego class inline.</li>
<li>Replace the DPI try/except block with a safer variant that doesn't reference <code>windll</code> outside the import scope.</li>
<li>Replace <code>_parse_dnd</code> to use <code>os.path.normpath</code> and handle braces &amp; spaces reliably.</li>
<li>Wrap all <code>Image.open</code> calls with context managers: <code>with Image.open(path) as img:</code></li>
<li>Use <code>logging</code> and <code>logger.exception</code> in broad excepts to retain tracebacks.</li>
</ul>

<pre><code># DPI block replacement
try:
    from ctypes import windll
    try:
        if hasattr(windll, 'shcore'):
            windll.shcore.SetProcessDpiAwareness(2)
        elif hasattr(windll, 'user32'):
            windll.user32.SetProcessDPIAware()
    except Exception:
        pass
except Exception:
    pass

# _parse_dnd replacement
@staticmethod
def _parse_dnd(data):
    raw = (data or '').strip()
    if raw.startswith('{') and '}' in raw:
        p = raw[1:raw.find('}')]
    else:
        p = raw.split()[0]
    p = p.strip('"').strip("'")
    return os.path.normpath(p)
</code></pre>

</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>Logging & error handling</h2>
<p>Add logging at top of modules and replace broad catches where possible:</p>

<pre><code>import logging
logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)
logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)

# Example inside an except:
except Exception as e:
    logger.exception('Embedding failed')
    return False, f'Embedding failed: {e}'
</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>KDF configurability</h2>
<p>Read scrypt parameters from environment variables to allow testing or tuning on low-end devices while keeping secure defaults.</p>
<pre><code>class KDF:
    SALT_LEN = 32
    _N = int(os.getenv('STEG_SCRYPT_N', 2**17))
    _r = int(os.getenv('STEG_SCRYPT_r', 8))
    _p = int(os.getenv('STEG_SCRYPT_p', 1))
</code></pre>
<p>Document the tradeoff in README: lowering <code>_N</code> reduces cost but weakens resistance to brute force.</p>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>CLI</h2>
<p>Add a small CLI module <code>cli.py</code> exposing subcommands: <code>hide</code>, <code>hide-plain</code>, and <code>extract</code>. Use <code>argparse</code> and call into <code>steg_core.Stego</code>.</p>

<pre><code># example usage
python -m stegtool.cli hide --image cover.png --in secret.txt --out stego.png --pw password
python -m stegtool.cli extract --image stego.png --out extracted.bin --pw password
</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>Tests</h2>
<p>Create <code>tests/test_steg_core.py</code>: generate a tiny in-memory image, hide/extract both plain and encrypted payloads and assert roundtrip equality. Set environment variables at test start to reduce scrypt cost for CI:</p>

<pre><code>import os
os.environ['STEG_SCRYPT_N'] = str(2**12)
os.environ['STEG_SCRYPT_r'] = '8'
os.environ['STEG_SCRYPT_p'] = '1'

# tests: test_hide_extract_text_encrypted, test_hide_extract_text_plain, test_hide_extract_file_encrypted
</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>CI</h2>
<p>Add <code>.github/workflows/ci.yml</code> to run tests. Ensure the test runner sets lower scrypt params for speed in CI.</p>

<pre><code>name: CI
on: [push, pull_request]
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v4
        with: python-version: '3.11'
      - run: python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
      - run: |
          export STEG_SCRYPT_N=$((2**12))
          pytest -q
</code></pre>
</div>

