<div class="section">
<h2>Acceptance criteria</h2>
<ul>
<li>Code builds and GUI runs manually.</li>
<li>Image file handles are not leaked (all opens use context managers).</li>
<li>Drag &amp; drop works for typical paths (Windows and POSIX) including paths with spaces.</li>
<li>Unit tests pass in CI (with lowered scrypt parameters).</li>
<li>Logging captures exceptions with tracebacks while UI shows friendly messages.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>PR description (suggestion)</h2>
<p>This PR extracts core steganography logic into <code>steg_core.py</code>, hardens file handling and DnD parsing, improves DPI handling on Windows, adds logging and configurable scrypt KDF parameters, and provides a CLI and unit tests. No wire-format change: still <code>&lt;|STEGv4|&gt;</code>. See commits for details.</p>
